                <pb facs="0739" n="735" sameAs="frus:frus1938v03/pg735"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/13356: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Chefoo</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Roberts</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chefoo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-07-01T10:00:00+08:00">July 1, 1938—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:44 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Japanese naval forces yesterday boarded Chinese Maritime Customs cruiser <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hai Cheng</hi> in Chefoo harbor and seized vessel
                    ordering British master and executive officer Theodore W. Joyce, American,
                    ashore. Chinese officers and crew were ordered to remain on board under penalty
                    court martial.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Embassy at Peiping and Hankow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Roberts</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
